(4462435, 642520, 89811, '<td valign="top">excellent - you arer drawn to "the eyes that have it !"</td>', 'excellent - you arer drawn to "the eyes that have it !"', '2008-02-06 01:53:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(4462447, 641749, 89811, '<td valign="top">I love it !  The colours are magnificent and so infinite</td>', 'I love it !  The colours are magnificent and so infinite', '2008-02-06 01:56:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(4462452, 641523, 84907, '<td valign="top">I like the way the high key lighting mixes with the intense eyes to really hook the viewer.  The intensity in the eyes is just very well done.  I am sure you will get lots of comments about the hair being in the eye.  For some that will be a welcome thing, and for some it will be a detractor.  For me it takes away from the eye, but not enough to mess up a good shot.  The only other area that I want to briefly touch on is the bottom right which looks to have some fairly serious JPG artifacts going on.  Specifically it looks pretty noisy.  My best guess is this is just a bi-product of the post processing.  Basic editing and full adjustments rather than selective will sometimes do that.  I love the idea and creativity and thank you for entering a very nice shot!</td>', 'I like the way the high key lighting mixes with the intense eyes to really hook the viewer.  The intensity in the eyes is just very well done.  I am sure you will get lots of comments about the hair being in the eye.  For some that will be a welcome thing, and for some it will be a detractor.  For me it takes away from the eye, but not enough to mess up a good shot.  The only other area that I want to briefly touch on is the bottom right which looks to have some fairly serious JPG artifacts going on.  Specifically it looks pretty noisy.  My best guess is this is just a bi-product of the post processing.  Basic editing and full adjustments rather than selective will sometimes do that.  I love the idea and creativity and thank you for entering a very nice shot!', '2008-02-06 01:57:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4462462, 643025, 84907, '<td valign="top">Fantastic with the eyes.  Great light, great angle to present them at, and a great idea with the white mummy strips to really set them off as well.  A couple of nitpicky things.  The top white strip actually leads my eye right to some eyebrow hair that wants to come poking out.  Also the bottom crop cuts it just a bit close to the bottom lid.  I am sure there were some compelling reasons to crop it that way, so both of those are pretty minimal and don''t really impact my score at all, but I always love getting other sets of eyes comments on my shots so figure I will try to do what I always hope for in comments.</td>', 'Fantastic with the eyes.  Great light, great angle to present them at, and a great idea with the white mummy strips to really set them off as well.  A couple of nitpicky things.  The top white strip actually leads my eye right to some eyebrow hair that wants to come poking out.  Also the bottom crop cuts it just a bit close to the bottom lid.  I am sure there were some compelling reasons to crop it that way, so both of those are pretty minimal and don''t really impact my score at all, but I always love getting other sets of eyes comments on my shots so figure I will try to do what I always hope for in comments.', '2008-02-06 02:01:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(4462470, 642860, 84907, '<td valign="top">Fantastic.  This is a great capture.  Excellently framed up with great depth of field.  The reflection was either exceptionally well planned or one heck of a great lucky break.  :-)  Trying to get any animal to work with you to get a shot like this is difficult and you should be commended greatly on a fantastic shot.</td>', 'Fantastic.  This is a great capture.  Excellently framed up with great depth of field.  The reflection was either exceptionally well planned or one heck of a great lucky break.  :-)  Trying to get any animal to work with you to get a shot like this is difficult and you should be commended greatly on a fantastic shot.', '2008-02-06 02:07:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(4462478, 643001, 84907, '<td valign="top">Haha  :)  Ok, instant pop factor with a nice tight shot like this, so great job there.  Also a great job of setting the glasses just right to avoid tons of flash reflection.  With a shot this close it is really difficult to keep from blowing things out all over the place and you did a great job keeping that under control.  I also really like the choice on depth of field as you can see the pink just start to fade away giving a very pleasing texture to the image.  I do think that the hair cutting into the eyes hurts the shot from a challenge point of view, but this picture is worth much more than that.  Great shot that I am sure you will enjoy for years.</td>', 'Haha  :)  Ok, instant pop factor with a nice tight shot like this, so great job there.  Also a great job of setting the glasses just right to avoid tons of flash reflection.  With a shot this close it is really difficult to keep from blowing things out all over the place and you did a great job keeping that under control.  I also really like the choice on depth of field as you can see the pink just start to fade away giving a very pleasing texture to the image.  I do think that the hair cutting into the eyes hurts the shot from a challenge point of view, but this picture is worth much more than that.  Great shot that I am sure you will enjoy for years.', '2008-02-06 02:13:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(4462492, 642688, 84907, '<td valign="top">Wow, I bet this took lots of frames.  I can''t even imagine the set up and trial and error.  So congrats there for sure.  Not sure what the black stuff is on the bottom eyelid, but I have itched my eye now at least 4 or 5 time while writing this comment.  :-)  The only real thing I have as a concern is that the refection that is so key in drawing in the viewer also is a bit busy for my eye and I get lost in it and lose the beauty of the actual eye (because it is a very pretty eye).  Great shot.</td>', 'Wow, I bet this took lots of frames.  I can''t even imagine the set up and trial and error.  So congrats there for sure.  Not sure what the black stuff is on the bottom eyelid, but I have itched my eye now at least 4 or 5 time while writing this comment.  :-)  The only real thing I have as a concern is that the refection that is so key in drawing in the viewer also is a bit busy for my eye and I get lost in it and lose the beauty of the actual eye (because it is a very pretty eye).  Great shot.', '2008-02-06 02:22:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(4462495, 642951, 84907, '<td valign="top">You have to love cat eyes.  :-)  Very nice capture.  I like the framing as well.  I will say that it takes a second to get oriented to the cat''s positioning and that can be a bit distracting, but the color and use of what appears to be natural light in a moving animal that never seems to want to cooperate is just plain excellent.  Well done.</td>', 'You have to love cat eyes.  :-)  Very nice capture.  I like the framing as well.  I will say that it takes a second to get oriented to the cat''s positioning and that can be a bit distracting, but the color and use of what appears to be natural light in a moving animal that never seems to want to cooperate is just plain excellent.  Well done.', '2008-02-06 02:25:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(4462509, 642453, 84907, '<td valign="top">Very nice job on this.  The moodiness of the lighting really works for me.  The depth of field is fantastic and I love the choice of background.  The bricks give it a street shot type of feel that just would never work as well with the moodiness of the look, the lighting, and the eyes if it were shot in a studio.  Focus is right on the money as are the catch lights in both eyes.  Fantastic shot.</td>', 'Very nice job on this.  The moodiness of the lighting really works for me.  The depth of field is fantastic and I love the choice of background.  The bricks give it a street shot type of feel that just would never work as well with the moodiness of the look, the lighting, and the eyes if it were shot in a studio.  Focus is right on the money as are the catch lights in both eyes.  Fantastic shot.', '2008-02-06 02:31:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(4462511, 642653, 84907, '<td valign="top">Nice shot.  Great use of the magnifying glass, and the lighting on the eye is fantastic.</td>', 'Nice shot.  Great use of the magnifying glass, and the lighting on the eye is fantastic.', '2008-02-06 02:32:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(4462515, 641268, 84907, '<td valign="top">Aww, cute kitty.  I think that the cat doesn''t seem to have wanted to work with you very well as he or she is loving whatever is below you and your lens.  :-)  Still a shot I am sure you will love for years to come.</td>', 'Aww, cute kitty.  I think that the cat doesn''t seem to have wanted to work with you very well as he or she is loving whatever is below you and your lens.  :-)  Still a shot I am sure you will love for years to come.', '2008-02-06 02:34:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(4462521, 640440, 84907, '<td valign="top">I like the shot.  Love the coloring.  I am sure it will be disqualified for the text in the bottom left, but great color and a great idea with the matching color on the top lid.</td>', 'I like the shot.  Love the coloring.  I am sure it will be disqualified for the text in the bottom left, but great color and a great idea with the matching color on the top lid.', '2008-02-06 02:36:09.000000', NULL, 1),
