(4485716, 642875, 74371, '<td valign="top">Congrats Judi!!! Maybe you should change your moniker to "Judi Blue"! :)<br/> <br/>And thank Kita for us too! She is a wonderful model for all that you do... and WE are the ones who reap the rewards! Such wonderful shots!!!<br/> <br/>But be careful, Judi! Some nasty UNknowing person could label you with child brutality. First you bend her up and around like a rubber Gumby:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=625835" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/792/120/625835.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/792/120/625835.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/792/120/625835.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>and now you festoon her with pretty stuff postponing her bedtime. Just kidding!!<br/> <br/>Way to go, Kiddo!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-14 02:32:29.</i></td>', 'Congrats Judi!!! Maybe you should change your moniker to "Judi Blue"! :) And thank Kita for us too! She is a wonderful model for all that you do... and WE are the ones who reap the rewards! Such wonderful shots!!! But be careful, Judi! Some nasty UNknowing person could label you with child brutality. First you bend her up and around like a rubber Gumby:  and now you festoon her with pretty stuff postponing her bedtime. Just kidding!! Way to go, Kiddo!!', '2008-02-14 02:31:21.000000', '2008-02-14 02:32:29.000000', 0),
(4486029, 642909, 39850, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 5.  Thought the light was very nice, but it wasn''t ''all about the eyes'' in my opinion, which I interpreted this Challenge to be.  Your style of entry was one of many who submitted more or less a portrait, which, as portraits should have, had good eye capture.  I think you made the right choice with this over your out-take.</td>', 'I gave this a 5.  Thought the light was very nice, but it wasn''t ''all about the eyes'' in my opinion, which I interpreted this Challenge to be.  Your style of entry was one of many who submitted more or less a portrait, which, as portraits should have, had good eye capture.  I think you made the right choice with this over your out-take.', '2008-02-14 09:08:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4486054, 642580, 81301, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gmarblestone:</b></div><hr/><i> Question.... i see that the outline of the bird is "fuzzy" and i wonder why?  The dof was 5.6 so that cant explain it.  So what does?  I didn''t vote in this challenge, but a 1 and a 2??? come on!  I think a crisper outline might have made the picture even better.  How do you think that could have been achieved? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thanks for your comment.<br/>the "fuzzy" outline is a result of a very shalow DOF. yes. the f was 5.6 but i was really close to the bird and the shot was taken with a 500mm lens.<br/>DOF determined by the f number + lens mm + distance from your subject. its not a fixed amount it changes...<br/> <br/>zohar</td>', 'Originally posted by gmarblestone: Question.... i see that the outline of the bird is "fuzzy" and i wonder why?  The dof was 5.6 so that cant explain it.  So what does?  I didn''t vote in this challenge, but a 1 and a 2??? come on!  I think a crisper outline might have made the picture even better.  How do you think that could have been achieved?   thanks for your comment.the "fuzzy" outline is a result of a very shalow DOF. yes. the f was 5.6 but i was really close to the bird and the shot was taken with a 500mm lens.DOF determined by the f number + lens mm + distance from your subject. its not a fixed amount it changes... zohar', '2008-02-14 09:36:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4486057, 642580, 81301, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MelonMusketeer:</b></div><hr/><i> Beautiful shot of a catalina macaw.  I like their little eyelashes.  This one looks almost exactly like my pet Jules. <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=476726" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/640/120/476726.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/640/120/476726.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/640/120/476726.jpg"/></a> </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>you have a BEAUTIFUL bird!!!<br/>i hope you two are having a lot of fun.<br/> <br/>thank you,<br/> <br/>zohar</td>', 'Originally posted by MelonMusketeer: Beautiful shot of a catalina macaw.  I like their little eyelashes.  This one looks almost exactly like my pet Jules.    you have a BEAUTIFUL bird!!!i hope you two are having a lot of fun. thank you, zohar', '2008-02-14 09:38:08.000000', NULL, 0),
